===Etymology===
From earlier {{inh|ja|ojp|-}} form {{ja-r|食ぶ|たぶ|to (humbly) receive or get|pos=from a superior}}, a verb with the {{ja-r|下二段|しも にだん|lower bigrade}} conjugation pattern. This was the [[humble]] form of {{ja-r|賜ぶ|たぶ|rom=-}}, {{ja-r|給ぶ|たぶ|to (deign to) give|pos=to an inferior}}, a verb with the full {{ja-r|四段|よだん|quadrigrade}} conjugation pattern.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten Concise|食}}</ref><ref name="DJR"/>
{{ja-from-shimonidan}}

Most likely related to {{ja-r|給う|たまう|to give|pos=as a superior gives a thing to, or does something for, an inferior}}.

Compare the historical development of meaning from “to humbly receive” → “to eat”, with the modern use of the humble verb {{ja-r|頂く|いただく|to receive}} just before eating, in a sense of “I humbly receive this food.”

