From {{inh|ja|ojp|-}}. First attested in the ''{{w|Kojiki}}'' of 712 {{CE}}.<ref name="KDJc">{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten Concise}}</ref> In turn, from {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|*mentu}}. Ryukyuan cognates support the existence of the first vowel having an initial mid vowel.

Possibly cognate with {{m|ja|瑞||tr=mizu|[[freshness]], [[youth]]}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|みず|acc=0|acc_ref=DJR}}
{{ja-accent-dialectal|region=Kyoto|k-0|みず|mízú}}
{{ja-accent-dialectal|region=Kagoshima|kt-a||み|づ|mídzù}}
{{rfap|ja}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|みず|hist=みづ}}

# [[water]] {{gloss|sometimes [[cold]] and/or [[fresh]]}}
#: {{syn|ja|ウオーター|tr=uōtā|ウォーター|tr2=wōtā|がっこ|tr3=gakko|q3=Tsugaru}}
#: {{ant|ja|湯|tr1=yu|pos1=specifically meaning "hot water"}}
#* {{RQ:Kokinshū}}
#*: {{ja-usex
|袖 ひちて むすび し '''水''' の こほれ る を 春 立つ けふ の 風 や とく らむ
|そで ひちて むすび し '''みづ''' の こほれ る を はる たつ けふ の かぜ や とく らむ
|During the coming spring, would the wind melt the '''water''' that I scooped out?
}}
# [[drinking water]]
#: {{syn|ja|飲水|tr=insui, nomimizu|飲用水|tr2=in'yōsui|飲料水|tr3=inryōsui}}
# a [[fluid]], [[liquid]]
#: {{syn|ja|液体|tr=ekitai}}
# a [[flood]]
#: {{syn|ja|大水|tr=ōmizu|洪水|tr2=kōzui|出水|tr3=shussui}}
# {{lb|ja|sumo}} {{short for|ja|水入り|tr=mizuiri}}: [[halt]]ing
# {{lb|ja|sumo}} {{short for|ja|力水|tr=chikara mizu}}: water [[offer]]ed to [[sumo]] [[wrestler]]s before a [[bout]]

====Usage notes====
* Note that, while ''mizu'' is the most general Japanese term for “{{m|en|water}}”, it does refer specifically to “{{m|en|[[water]] that is not [[hot]]}}”.  Meanwhile, the word {{m|ja|湯|tr=yu}} refers specifically to “{{m|en|hot water}}”.  Consider {{m|ja|水風呂||tr=mizu-buro|[[cold]]-[[water]] [[bath]]}}, contrasting with {{m|ja|風呂||tr=furo|pos=implying hot water|[[bath]]}}.

